# Copy this file to onboarding/.env and fill in real values. onboarding/.env
# is gitignored. Credentials and identity ONLY -- operational settings (the
# service's own public URL) live in .env.config -- see .env.config.example.
# An agent must never open this file; see root CLAUDE.md's "Secret handling"
# section.
#
# This is a separate service from app/ (the review engine) -- its own
# deploy, its own env vars, no shared credential-handling code path (see
# onboarding/CLAUDE.md). Unlike app/, onboarding/ has no scripts/deploy.py
# sync logic of its own, so this split is a lighter-weight convention here
# (operator-facing organization, secrets-needing-care vs. safe-to-view-and-
# edit-freely) rather than something enforced by a test or a config-sync
# script.

# --- Server-side wizard session store ---
# onboarding/ used to be a fully stateless relay (no DB, no server-side
# secret storage) -- that invariant was found to be fragile against mobile
# browsers destroying sessionStorage mid-flow (see ISSUES.md) and was
# deliberately dropped. A visitor's in-progress wizard session -- including
# their submitted credentials -- now lives in its own dedicated Postgres
# (a separate Supabase project from any visitor's own provisioned project,
# and separate from bot/'s queue DB -- see onboarding/CLAUDE.md's "own
# threat model" rule), encrypted at the application layer before it's
# written.
#
# DATABASE_URL: connection string for onboarding/'s own dedicated Postgres
# (create a new Supabase project for this -- do not reuse bot/'s queue DB
# or a visitor's provisioned project).
DATABASE_URL=
#
# ONBOARDING_SESSION_ENCRYPTION_KEY: a Fernet key (44 base64 chars, e.g.
# `python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"`)
# used to encrypt every credential value inside a session row before it's
# written to DATABASE_URL, and decrypt it only in-process when a server
# action needs the raw value. Losing/rotating this key makes every existing
# session's stored credentials unrecoverable (visitors just restart the
# wizard -- sessions are short-lived by design, see the session TTL in
# onboarding/CLAUDE.md).
ONBOARDING_SESSION_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Supabase OAuth app (sub-project 3: Supabase provisioning frame) ---
# This service's first operator-level secrets -- set once, never visitor-
# supplied. Register the OAuth app manually (Supabase has no self-
# registration mechanism, unlike GitHub's App Manifest flow): Supabase
# organization settings -> OAuth Apps -> Add application, redirect URI
# {your deployed origin}/oauth/supabase/callback (a bare path -- Supabase
# matches registered redirect URIs exactly, and this page derives its own
# origin from location.origin, so there's no separate base-URL setting to
# keep in sync here). Copy the resulting client_id/client_secret here.
# See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-26-onboarding-supabase-provisioning-frame-design.md
# section 8.
SUPABASE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
SUPABASE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# More credentials land here as later sub-projects (LLM provider UI,
# UptimeRobot, Render service creation) are built -- none needed yet.
